omx-panel (0.17.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * CHANGELOG.md: the 0.17.1 line the release proof reads
  * release: omx-panel 0.17.1 (0.17.0 to 0.17.1), a patch
  * release: the RPMs build for Fedora aarch64 too, not x86_64 alone (#274)
  * Package builds skip the shape renders by name: ci.yml and the release
    proof run them (#270)
  * base: BUILT_FROM is BUILT_FROM.txt, a one-value file the SPDX check reads
    as data (#268)
  * release: the proof runs the shape generators at ci.yml's pin (#266)
  * release: the proof links the twins where the packages install them, under
    /usr (#264)
  * The tree reads the channel's omx-dsp and omx-contract after npm ci, as
    the installed package does (#262)
  * release: a devel push's proof reads the staging channel its build was
    staged to (#260)
  * release: the RPM is x86_64 only, as the build requirements it is built
    against are
  * Fix: the dirty-rectangle spectrum test hands the spectrum as devel takes
    it
  * store tests: the plugin-db fixture domain states its format
  * docs, tests: two lines state the fact, not a place a reader cannot open
  * packaging: the domains are listed under %{omx_contract_dir}
  * Fix: the ui library keeps its own version, libomx-panel-ui.so.0
  * contract: the contract directory has no schema-major level
  * domains: every domain is at 0.1.0, its vocabulary own version, never the
    package one
  * Fix: the shapes follow the wave: the parity scripts' new place, and a
    code of four parts
  * Fix: the group model keeps the wave's own changes; only the unit hunk is
    #250's
  * release: a merge to devel publishes the real package to staging
  * docs/renderer.md: the spectrum signature's change names no release (it is
    unreleased; the tree is 0.16.2)
  * test: the contract package's one direct install is omx-panel's own
    transaction, and the proof runs after it
  * runtime-install-check: omx-panel's requirement on omx-panel-contract is
    met by the package this build made
  * test: a requirement on omx-panel-contract is met by the package this
    build made (red: the check asks the channel)
  * packaging: the dependency on omx-contract-data states no version (no
    hand-kept floor)
  * test: the hostd name guard reads the files again (tree-grep.mjs), as
    devel has it since #207
  * 0.16.2: the role table names omx-contract 3.22.0's unit ids (#256)
  * #170 consumers: the role table names coef where it named x, one for one
  * #170 consumers: red first, the plain multiplier is coef: the compressor's
    ratio in coef keeps its role
  * V23d (P2): two comments stop naming the param-contract unit table
  * servedUnit reads omx-contract's PARAM_UNITS_CLAP_ENCODED (#256)
  * V23d (P2): red first, a unit is served when omx-contract's
    PARAM_UNITS_CLAP_ENCODED holds its id
  * tests: the last readers of a floor; the rules are version 5, describe's
    output having moved with the folds (#239)
  * panel_codes.h: the store codes are nine (#239)
  * panel domain: each store code's x-code is its place (#239)
  * store: a domain is opened as installed, with no floor; a descriptor that
    refers to nothing states no requires (#239)
  * No hand-kept floors: our packages are named without a version, and a
    subpackage at the version built with it (#239)
  * tests: no version relation on a package of ours is typed by hand (red,
    #239)
  * meaning-infer: a unit is its standard id, read from the vocabulary (#251)
  * test: meaning-infer reads a unit as its standard id, never a spelled word
    (red, #251)
  * ci.yml: a pull request into devel may take its packages from the staging
    channel
  * group model: a unit's token is its standard id, read from the vocabulary
    (#74)
  * test: the group model's unit tokens are the vocabulary's (red, #74)
  * install-under-test: the files are compared by sha256sum, which every
    image has (cmp is diffutils')
  * runtime install: the contract package under test goes over any channel
    copy and is proven to be what is installed (#248)
  * tests: the runtime install check installs the package file it is given,
    over any channel copy (red, #248)
  * install-contract: the panel and gestures domains are installed as
    omx-panel
  * look-roles: the knob pointer's floor is measured on the knob face, in
    every finish of the pin (#244)
  * docs: a floor's ground may be a key a finish sets; the knob pointer is
    read on the knob face (#244)
  * .githooks/commit-msg is the shared stub, byte for byte
  * renderer test: the install check stages what is built and builds nothing
  * changelog: the renderer's ABI break, libomx-panel-render.so.1 and the new
    set_spectrum
  * renderer: the spectrum's pre, both and delta goldens cut again on devel
  * renderer: the spectrum's two taps, the console's modes and the delta
  * renderer: the shared library's soname moves to libomx-panel-render.so.1
  * test: the spectrum's two taps, its modes and the delta, red first
  * docs: the spectrum takes both taps, the console's modes and the delta
  * panel-layout: the delay example's pingpong takes its role, its meaning
    stated since omx-contract 3.22.0
  * docs: looks: state the console's facts instead of pointing into its tree
    (#237)
  * docs: looks: accepted; the ten decisions ruled and the body written to
    them (#237)
  * docs: looks: the coordinator's recommendation beside each open decision
